<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        The <a href="/dmx">DMX Desk</a> controls the venue's lighting through a kiosk's DMX output. It needs the
        Admin or CanManageDmxSystems role. Choose the kiosk at the top left. Kiosks that are switched off show as
        <strong>(offline)</strong>: you can still set up their fixtures and scenes, and the desk remembers the kiosk
        you used last.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Fixtures and Channels">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Fixtures</strong> shows each light as a card: a circle in the light's current colour, a
                <strong>Brightness</strong> slider, a <strong>Colour</strong> picker with quick colours, and
                <strong>Pan</strong> and <strong>Tilt</strong> for moving heads. <strong>Off</strong> and
                <strong>Full</strong> set the brightness at once, and <strong>Channels</strong> opens that light's raw faders.</li>
            <li><strong>Channels</strong> shows raw faders 32 at a time. Use the arrows or the list to change bank, or
                <strong>By fixture</strong> to see one light's channels together. The tag above a fader says what it
                controls; an amber <strong>2×</strong> means two fixtures share that channel.</li>
            <li>The desk always follows the lights, so you see a running scene or someone else's changes as they happen.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Live and Blind">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Live</strong>: the faders drive the lights straight away.</li>
            <li><strong>Blind</strong>: change the desk without the lights following. An amber bar reminds you.
                Press <strong>Send to lights</strong> when you're ready, or <strong>Discard changes</strong> to go back
                to what the lights are showing. Going back to Live with unsent changes asks whether to send them.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Master, Blackout and Lock">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Master</strong> dims every light together. It only changes brightness: moving heads don't
                move and colours don't change. The faders keep their own levels.</li>
            <li><strong>Blackout</strong> turns every light off at once. Press <strong>Bring lights back</strong> to
                return exactly to how they were, including anything you changed while it was on.</li>
            <li><strong>Lock</strong> stops the faders and buttons being moved by accident. The desk starts locked on
                phones and tablets. Blackout and stopping scenes still work while locked.</li>
            <li>Lanyard remembers each kiosk's lights, master and blackout. If the kiosk or Lanyard restarts, the
                lights come back as they were.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Which output the kiosk uses">
        <FluentText>
            On <a href="/manage/clients">Clients</a>, open the kiosk's <strong>Settings</strong>, go to the
            <strong>DMX</strong> tab and pick the device under <strong>Use this Device</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
